Description: SAST and SCA security scanner
 argus scans source code and dependency manifests for security issues.
 It combines a built-in Java dataflow engine, Semgrep rule packs for
 Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, Go, PHP, C/C++ and Ruby, OSV-based
 dependency checks, secret detection and infrastructure-as-code
 heuristics.
 .
 Reports are available as JSON, SARIF, Markdown, text, CycloneDX/SPDX
 SBOM and OpenVEX. Baseline files, suppressions, quality gates and
 EPSS/KEV enrichment support use in CI pipelines.
 .
 The package is architecture independent.  On installation it creates a
 private Python environment in /var/lib/argus-scanner/runtime and
 downloads the scanner dependencies, including the latest Semgrep release,
 from the Python package index.  For machines without network access, the
 runtime can be provisioned from a local wheel directory with
 argus-setup-runtime --wheelhouse.
